{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '500,525p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '655,685p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | sed -n '1680,1707p'\"","aggregated_output":"   500\t\n   501\t   A parked entry is stored as the builder left it plus, for a writer, the\n   502\t   `:datom` it retries: registers and resource ids only. Neither the live\n   503\t   stream handle nor a restore closure is attached — `check-wait-set`\n   504\t   resolves handles from the store at every poll, and the scheduler that pops\n   505\t   a woken entry dispatches restoration itself — so a blocked entry is pure\n   506\t   data and survives serialization.\"\n   507\t  [state effect {:keys [park-entry-fns], :as opts}]\n   508\t  (let [park-entry (get park-entry-fns (:effect effect))\n   509\t        result\n   510\t        (case (:effect effect)\n   511\t          :vm/store-put {:state (assoc state\n   512\t                                       :store (assoc (:store state)\n   513\t                                                     (:key effect)\n   514\t                                                     (:val effect))),\n   515\t                         :value (:val effect),\n   516\t                         :blocked? false}\n   517\t          :stream/make\n   518\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \"stream\")\n   519\t                [stream-ref new-state] (handle-make s' effect id)]\n   520\t            {:state new-state, :value stream-ref, :blocked? false})\n   521\t          :stream/cursor\n   522\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \"cursor\")\n   523\t                [cursor-ref new-state] (handle-cursor s' effect id)]\n   524\t            {:state new-state, :value cursor-ref, :blocked? false})\n   525\t          :stream/put\n   655\t  \"Record one loaded image's address in the `address → local-id` alias\n   656\t   column (UCF §7.3.4). The column is che