{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc | sed -n '36,55p;205,232p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc | sed -n '35,58p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/completion.cljc | sed -n '687,707p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '1175,1205p'\"","aggregated_output":"    36\t;; =============================================================================\n    37\t\n    38\t(def contract-stamp\n    39\t  \"The complete execution contract a canonical vector is interpreted under:\n    40\t   `:yin.code/contract` names the published revision of the tuple grammar,\n    41\t   S2.6 rules, last-value-wins resolution, opcode table, transitions,\n    42\t   resolution precedence, effect outcomes and scheduler\n    43\t   (`yin.vm.semantic.md` S2.4); `:yin.k/version` is this envelope's own\n    44\t   version. A resumer on another revision answers `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`\n    45\t   before lowering; a code index is keyed per stamp.\"\n    46\t  {:yin.code/contract \"v2\",\n    47\t   :yin.k/version 0})\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\t;; =============================================================================\n    51\t;; The canonical instruction vector (S7.3.2)\n    52\t;; =============================================================================\n    53\t\n    54\t(def ^:private segment-attrs\n    55\t  \"Segment-entity attributes the canonical form folds away or excludes:\n   205\t   UCF mints no second addressing scheme.\"\n   206\t  [v]\n   207\t  (jing/segment-key v))\n   208\t\n   209\t\n   210\t(defn canonicalize\n   211\t  \"Code identity as one S7.9 outcome. On success\n   212\t   `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/ok, :yin.code/vector v, :yin.code/hash address,\n   213\t   :yin.k/contract contract-stamp}`; otherwise the `refusal` map the\n   214\t   vector function would have thrown.\"\n   215\t  [datoms]\n   216\t  (try\n   217\t    (let [v (batch->canonical-instruction-vector datoms)