e (get transitions mnem)\n   299\t      :step (if (= :closure mnem)\n   300\t              [[(inc pc) bound] [(nth t 2) (into bound (nth t 1))]]\n   301\t              [[(inc pc) bound]])\n   302\t      :parking [[(inc pc) bound]]\n   303\t      :jump [[(nth t 1) bound]]\n   304\t      :branch [[(inc pc) bound] [(nth t 1) bound]]\n   305\t      [])))\n   306\t\n   307\t\n   308\t(defn lexically-required\n   309\t  \"The names the code reachable from `pc` reads from E, from the vector\n   310\t   alone (S7.4.2): every `:var` name on a control path from `pc` --\n   311\t   through fall-through, jumps, branches, and the bodies of closures\n   312\t   created on the way -- minus the names those closures bind. Callees are\n   313\t   values, not code reachable here: a closure already on the stack carries\n   314\t   its own captured environment, which is the frame's business. Sorted by\n   315\t   name so the result is a stable value.\"\n   316\t  [v pc]\n   317\t  (loop [work [[pc #{}]]\n   318\t         seen #{}\n   319\t         names #{}]\n   320\t    (if-let [[p bound :as item] (peek work)]\n   321\t      (let [work (pop work)]\n   322\t        (if (contains? seen item)\n   323\t          (recur work seen names)\n   324\t          (let [t (nth v p)\n   325\t                names (if (and (= :var (nth t 0))\n   326\t                               (not (contains? bound (nth t 1))))\n   327\t                        (conj names (nth t 1))\n   328\t                        names)]\n   329\t            (recur (into work (successors v p bound))\n   330\t                   (conj seen item)\n   331\t                   names))))\n   332\t      (vec (sort-by str names)))))\n   333\t\n   334\t\n   335\t(defn safepoints\n   336\t  \"The static safepoint map of one canonical vector (S7.4.2): one entry per\n   337\t   parking instruction, each carrying only what the vector alone fixes --\n   338\t   the parking pc, the canonical resume pc (pc+1, always inside the segment\n   339\t   by S2.6), the reasons under which the machine parks there, the stack\n   340\t   effect across the instruction, and the lexically required names at the\n   341\t   resume pc. Absolute depth, activation bases, captured environments and\n   342\t   physical layouts are not here: they ride in the frame\n   343\t   (`activation-state`).\"\n   344\t  [v]\n   345\t  (into []\n   346\t        (keep-indexed\n   347\t          (fn [pc t]\n   348\t            (when (= :parking (get transitions (nth t 0)))\n   349\t              {:yin.safepoint/at pc,\n   350\t               :yin.safepoint/pc (inc pc),\n   351\t               :yin.safepoint/reasons (get parking-reasons (nth t 0)),\n   352\t               :yin.safepoint/stack-effect (stack-effect t),\n   353\t               :yin.safepoint/lexically-required\n   354\t               (lexically-required v (inc pc))})))\n   355\t        v))\n   356\t\n   357\t\n   358\t(defn safepoint-table\n   359\t  \"`safepoints` published per segment, keyed by the code's address and the\n   360\t   engine profile that derived it (the reference machine by default).\"\n   361\t  ([v] (safepoint-table v :yin.vm.semantic/reference))\n   362\t  ([v engine]\n   363\t   {:yin.safepoint/segment (code-address v),\n   364\t    :yin.safepoint/engine engine,\n   365\t    :yin.safepoint/safepoints (safepoints v)}))\n   366\t\n   367\t\n   368\t(defn safepoint-at\n   369\t  \"The static safepoint entry whose canonical resume pc is `pc`, or the\n   370\t   S7.9 `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` outcome naming the pc.\"\n   371\t  [v pc]\n   372\t  (or (some #(when (= pc (:yin.safepoint/pc %)) %) (safepoints v))\n   373\t      {:yin.k/status :yin.k/not-at-safepoint, :yin.k/pc pc}))\n   374\t\n   375\t\n   376\t(defn activation-state\n   377\t  \"The dynamic half of a parked configuration, read off a frame -- a wait\n   378\t   entry or parked record `{segment pc env stack k}` -- never derived from\n   379\t   code: the absolute operand-stack depth, the names E actually binds, and\n   380\t   each return frame's activation base.\"\n   381\t  [frame]\n   382\t  {:yin.k/depth (count (:stack frame)),\n   383\t   :yin.k/bound (vec (sort-by str (keys (:env frame)))),\n   384\t   :yin.k/stack-bases (mapv :stack-base (:k frame))})\n   385\t\n   386\t\n   387\t(defn unsatisfied-names\n   388\t  \"The lexically required names of a static safepoint that the frame's\n   389\t   environment does not bind and that `resolvable` (store, primitives,\n   390\t   modules -- the rest of `resolve-var`'s order) does not answer: the\n   391\t   conformance check that a frame carries what its code will read.\"\n   392\t  [safepoint frame resolvable]\n   393\t  (vec (remove (fn [n]\n   394\t                 (or (contains? (:env frame) n) (resolvable n)))\n   395\t               (:yin.safepoint/lexically-required safepoint))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:43:   `{:yin.code/contract \\\"v2\\\", :yin.k/version 0}`. A `:derive` record\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:48:   :yin.code/contract \"v2\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:82:(defn derive-lowering\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:170:      :yin.k/profile-mismatch :record <p> :implemented <p>}` and\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:199:             {:kind :yin.k/profile-mismatch\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc:15:     it is interpreted under is `contract-stamp`. `canonicalize` bundles\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc:38:(def contract-stamp\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc:40:   `:yin.code/contract` names the published revision of the tuple grammar,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc:44:   version. A resumer on another revision answers `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc:46:  {:yin.code/contract \"v2\",\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc:213:   :yin.k/contract contract-stamp}`; otherwise the `refusal` map the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc:221:       :yin.k/contract contract-stamp})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
