th node]` tuple per place, so a structurally shared subtree\n  1304\t   (§4.4) yields one tuple per place and one node id. Computed by the same\n  1305\t   walk as the projection, so it is generic over every §2.3 tag. It is a\n  1306\t   pure function of the tree and carries no origin; a query fixes origin\n  1307\t   from the composition's side and joins on `[root path]` (§6.1). Assumes\n  1308\t   the walk terminates: projected ids are content addresses of their\n  1309\t   children, so a projected set is acyclic by construction (§4.1).\"\n  1310\t  [{:keys [root rows]}]\n  1311\t  (loop [frontier [[[] root]]\n  1312\t         tuples []]\n  1313\t    (if (empty? frontier)\n  1314\t      (set tuples)\n  1315\t      (let [children (mapcat (fn [[path id]]\n  1316\t                               (let [row (get rows id)]\n  1317\t                                 (map (fn [[step cid]] [(conj path step) cid])\n  1318\t                                      (when row (occurrence-child-places row)))))\n  1280\t\n  1281\t;; =============================================================================\n  1282\t;; Expander observer (§9)\n  1283\t;; =============================================================================\n  1284\t\n  1285\t(defn make-expander\n  1286\t  \"The observer consumer: `ctx`, the `program-out` writer, and an optional\n  1287\t   log writer, with nothing staged.\"\n  1288\t  ([ctx out] (make-expander ctx out nil))\n  1289\t  ([ctx out log]\n  1290\t   {:ctx ctx, :out out, :out-staged nil, :log log, :log-staged nil,\n  1291\t    :forwarded 0, :errors []}))\n  1292\t\n  1293\t\n  1294\t(defn ready?\n  1295\t  \"Ready only when both staged slots are empty.\"\n  1296\t  [expander]\n  1297\t  (and (nil? (:out-staged expander)) (nil? (:log-staged expander))))\n  1298\t\n  1299\t\n  1300\t(defn load\n  1301\t  \"Expand one observed batch once: keep the returned context, stage the tree\n  1302\t   only on success, stage the log when a log writer exists, and accumulate\n  1303\t   the error of a failed expansion. Expansion failure is data, so the\n  1304\t   cursor advances past it.\"\n  1305\t  [expander batch]\n  1306\t  (let [{:keys [status tree log error ctx]} (expand-batch batch (:ctx expander))]\n  1307\t    (cond-> (assoc expander :ctx ctx)\n  1308\t      (= :ok status) (assoc :out-staged tree)\n  1309\t      (:log expander) (assoc :log-staged log)\n  1310\t      (= :error status) (update :errors conj error))))\n  1311\t\n  1312\t\n  1313\t(defn- flush-slot\n  1314\t  [expander writer-key slot-key on-ok]\n  1315\t  (if-let [payload (get expander slot-key)]\n   400\t\n   401\t\n   402\t(defn lower-ast\n   403\t  \"`lower` ∘ `yin.vm/ast->datoms`. Unsupported nodes are rejected here\n   404\t   first, because `ast->datoms` cannot represent them.\"\n   405\t  ([ast] (lower-ast ast {}))\n   406\t  ([ast opts]\n   407\t   (doseq [node (tree-seq map? ast-children ast)]\n   408\t     (reject-unsupported! (:type node) node))\n   409\t   (lower (vm/ast->datoms ast (select-keys opts [:t])) opts)))\n   410\t\n   411\t\n   412\t(defn ast-loader\n   413\t  \"Adapt a code loader `(fn [vm code-datoms])` into one for a program stream\n   414\t   carrying AST datoms: §3.1's `(comp vm-load-program lower)` for a binary\n   415\t   loader. The composition makes this choice; no evaluator learns which form\n   416\t   travels.\n   417\t\n   418\t   Successive batches on one medium are independent AST programs whose\n   419\t   tempids restart, so the default `:id-start` would hand two programs of\n   420\t   the same size one segment id, which the loader rejects as a conflict. Each\n   421\t   batch is therefore lowered below the input and below every segment the VM\n   422\t   already holds under `:code`; closures and continuations naming earlier\n   423\t   segments keep resolving.\"\n   424\t  [load-program]\n   425\t  (fn [vm datoms]\n   426\t    (let [floor (reduce min\n   427\t                        (min (- datom/first-user-id) (vm/loaded-code-floor (:code vm)))\n   428\t                        (map first datoms))]\n   429\t      (load-program vm (lower datoms {:id-start (dec floor)})))))\n   430\t\n   431\t\n   432\t(defn rows-loader\n   433\t  \"Adapt a vector loader (`semantic/load-vector`) into the row lane's loader\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
